                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="803-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_xy.png" width=27 height=27 alt="X/Y Stereo" title="X/Y Stereo" ></span>beyerdynamic MCE 72</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    X/Y Stereo Condenser Stereo Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The MCE 72 is a stereo FET condenser, with two miniature electret condenser capsules mounted at 120&deg; for XY-stereo recording.</p><p>The mic was designed to be used with portable handheld recorder and video cameras, and as such includes a cable that allows the mic to be plugged into a 3.5mm stereo audio input jack.</p><p><img src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/mic_extras/beyerdynamic/mce-72-circuit.jpg" width="100" alt="MCE 72 Circuit" class="thumb shaft" />The mic is available in three versions:</p><ul><li><b>MCE 72</b> - powered by 1.5V AA battery. Mic body is 196mm long.</li><li><b>MCE 72 CAM</b> - same as MCE 72, but includes different accessories (see below). Mic body is 196mm long.</li><li><b>MCE 72 PV CAM</b>Phantom powered (11&ndash;52V). Mic body is 136mm long.</li></ul><p>The MCE 72 kit is supplied with a hard mount (p/n MKV 108) and a 3.5mm conversion cable (XLR5M to 3.5mm stereo male; p/n MKV 82-K3). </p><p>The MCE 72 CAM includes an elastic suspension with a hotshoe flash mount (p/n EA 86) for mounting the mic to a video camera. It also includes a foam windscreen (p/n WS 72) and a 35cm XLR5M-to-3.5mm stereo cable.</p><p>The MCE 72 PV CAM (the phantom-powered version of the mic) includes EA 86 hotshoe shockmount as described above, a foam windscreen, and a half-meter 3.5mm conversion cable (p/n MVK 82-N(CM)).<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/beyerdynamic/MCE-72">beyerdynamic MCE 72</a> is also known as: MCE72, MCE 72 PV CAM, MCE 72 CAM.</p>
